# Architecture Boundaries

Use clear ownership boundaries for all frontend architecture work.

## Rule

- Route segments in `frontend/app/**` own data fetching, orchestration, and route-level composition.
- Shared presentational UI belongs in `frontend/app/components/**`.
- Data normalization and adapters belong in `frontend/app/lib/**` or `frontend/sanity/lib/**`.
- Avoid passing raw CMS query shapes directly into reusable presentational components.
- Keep client/server boundaries explicit (`*.client.tsx` for client components).

## Quick Checks

- If a component calls `sanityFetch` or route-only logic, keep it in route scope.
- If UI is reused across routes and has no fetch/orchestration concerns, extract to a shared component.
- If a shape conversion is needed, place it in a mapper/adapter utility, not in shared UI.
